 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Initial Device Performance Prediction (JV Default PCE)\n",
    "\n",
    "## 1. Introduction\n",
    "Predicting the initial Power Conversion Efficiency ($PCE$) of a device based on its architecture and material composition is vital for rapid prototyping. This notebook focuses on the **JV Default PCE** prediction.\n",
    "\n",
    "## 2. Methodology\n",
    "*   **Target:** Initial efficiency as measured by J-V characteristic sweeps.\n",
    "*   **Features:** Layer sequences (ETL/HTL), device architecture (nip/pin), and perovskite band gap."
   ],
   "id": "intro"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import joblib\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import r2_score, mean_absolute_error\n",
    "\n",
    "# EXPLICIT WHITE THEME\n",
    "import matplotlib as mpl\n",
    "mpl.rcParams['figure.facecolor'] = 'white'\n",
    "mpl.rcParams['axes.facecolor'] = 'white'\n",
    "mpl.rcParams['savefig.facecolor'] = 'white'\n",
    "sns.set_theme(style=\"white\", palette=\"Set2\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Load device performance data\n",
    "df_jv = pd.read_parquet('../data/solar_panels.parquet').dropna(subset=['JV_default_PCE'])\n",
    "model_pce = joblib.load('../ml_models/pce_jv_model.joblib')\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Dataset contains {len(df_jv)} unique device configurations.\")"
   ],
   "id": "load"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Architecture Impact Analysis\n",
    "Does the choice between **n-i-p** and **p-i-n** architecture fundamentally change the efficiency ceiling?"
   ],
   "id": "arch_md"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6), facecolor='white')\n",
    "ax = sns.boxplot(data=df_jv, x='Cell_architecture', y='JV_default_PCE', palette='Set2')\n",
    "ax.set_facecolor(\"white\")\n",
    "plt.title(\"Efficiency Distribution by Device Architecture\", fontsize=14)\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"Architecture\", fontsize=12)\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Initial PCE (%)\", fontsize=12)\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ],
   "id": "arch_plot"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Prediction Accuracy\n",
    "Visualizing the model's ability to predict device efficiency across different stacks."
   ],
   "id": "eval_md"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "features = [\n",
    "    'A_1', 'A_2', 'A_3', 'B_1', 'C_1', 'C_2',\n",
    "    'en_A', 'en_B', 'en_C', 'mass_A', 'mass_B', 'mass_C',\n",
    "    'tolerance_factor', 'octahedral_factor', 'is_2d', 'dimension', 'space_group',\n",
    "    'Cell_architecture', 'ETL_stack_sequence', 'HTL_stack_sequence', 'Backcontact_stack_sequence', \n",
    "    'Cell_area_measured', 'Perovskite_band_gap', \n",
    "    'composition_inorganic'\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "y_true = df_jv['JV_default_PCE']\n",
    "y_pred = model_pce.predict(df_jv[features])\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(6, 6), facecolor='white')\n",
    "plt.scatter(y_true, y_pred, alpha=0.4, color='#16a085')\n",
    "plt.plot([0, 30], [0, 30], 'k--', lw=1.5)\n",
    "plt.gca().set_facecolor(\"white\")\n",
    "plt.title(f\"Device Performance Parity (R² = {r2_score(y_true, y_pred):.3f})\", fontsize=14)\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"Experimental PCE (%)\", fontsize=12)\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Predicted PCE (%)\", fontsize=12)\n",
    "plt.xlim(0, 26)\n",
    "plt.ylim(0, 26)\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ],
   "id": "parity"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Conclusion\n",
    "The XGBoost model captures the complex interplay between material composition and stack sequence. This model serves as the primary evaluation engine in our **Inverse Design** pipeline, enabling the search for high-efficiency device architectures."
   ],
   "id": "conclusion"
  }
 ],
